1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,532
This video shows what is special about importing and exporting contacts:

2
00:00:05,532 --> 00:00:10,414
how the import skips duplicate phone numbers, how it reads local phone numbers

3
00:00:10,414 --> 00:00:16,050
with the right country, and how an export can carry each contact's last completed activity.

4
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:25,028
A contact is called and texted, so the same phone number twice means

5
00:00:25,028 --> 00:00:27,750
the same person twice in your call list.

6
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,043
A list from a spreadsheet often has people you already have, or the

7
00:00:33,043 --> 00:00:34,910
same person on two rows.

8
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:41,420
So the contact import can skip duplicates, and reads local numbers with the country you choose.

9
00:00:45,622 --> 00:00:48,545
Open Content, Import, and choose Contact.

10
00:00:48,545 --> 00:00:51,096
A contact type adds import options.

11
00:00:51,096 --> 00:00:54,579
Ignore duplicate by phone number is on by default.

12
00:00:54,579 --> 00:00:58,187
It imports only the first row for each phone number.

13
00:00:58,187 --> 00:01:03,350
Later duplicates in the file, and numbers that already exist in the database,

14
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:06,212
are skipped and added to the error file.

15
00:01:06,662 --> 00:01:10,398
Compare with decides which records count as existing:

16
00:01:10,398 --> 00:01:15,147
every contact, only contacts of this type, or every contact and lead.

17
00:01:15,147 --> 00:01:19,263
Leads are left out by default, so a customer who was once a

18
00:01:19,263 --> 00:01:21,352
lead can still be imported.

19
00:01:21,803 --> 00:01:25,708
Lead country is the country that local phone numbers belong to.

20
00:01:25,708 --> 00:01:30,067
A number that is not in international format is read with this country,

21
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:35,161
so keep one country per file unless every number is already in international format.

22
00:01:35,161 --> 00:01:39,463
The same numbers are used to infer a time zone when the file has none.

23
00:01:39,914 --> 00:01:41,177
Upload the file.

24
00:01:41,177 --> 00:01:45,080
Here, two new people are imported, and three rows are skipped:

25
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:49,329
one has the number of an existing contact, one repeats a number from

26
00:01:49,329 --> 00:01:53,175
the file, and one has the number of another existing contact.

27
00:01:53,175 --> 00:01:56,734
The skipped rows are in the error file, with the reason.

28
00:02:00,927 --> 00:02:05,123
Open Content, Export, and choose the Contact type.

29
00:02:05,123 --> 00:02:11,267
Besides the usual filters, a contact type shows a CRM last activity section.

30
00:02:11,718 --> 00:02:16,879
Tick Include last completed activity information, and choose a subject, and the file

31
00:02:16,879 --> 00:02:21,237
appends each contact's most recent completed activity of that subject:

32
00:02:21,237 --> 00:02:26,971
the agent's note, the completion date, the disposition, the subject, and the subject's fields.

33
00:02:26,971 --> 00:02:31,387
Tick Include only contacts with a last activity record to leave out the

34
00:02:31,387 --> 00:02:33,107
contacts that have none.

35
00:02:33,107 --> 00:02:36,318
This is a quick way to prepare the next call list.

36
00:02:40,518 --> 00:02:45,645
A contact import can also check each number against the national do-not-call registries

37
00:02:45,645 --> 00:02:46,858
you have set up.

38
00:02:47,608 --> 00:02:52,364
Rows the import leaves out on purpose are counted as errors, with the

39
00:02:52,364 --> 00:02:55,218
reason, so nothing disappears silently.

40
00:02:55,968 --> 00:03:00,254
A lead import has the same checks, plus its own options such as

41
00:03:00,254 --> 00:03:02,738
the list name and the lead status.

42
00:03:06,938 --> 00:03:11,788
Load a purchased or exported list without creating duplicate people.

43
00:03:12,538 --> 00:03:14,698
Clean up a list before calling it.

44
00:03:15,448 --> 00:03:19,428
Get the last result of every contact into a spreadsheet.

45
00:03:20,178 --> 00:03:23,318
Prepare the next call list from the last outcome.

46
00:03:25,318 --> 00:03:29,941
Skip the duplicates, set the country, and export the last activity, so your

47
00:03:29,941 --> 00:03:33,366
contact list stays clean and your calls stay targeted.

48
00:03:33,366 --> 00:03:37,704
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

49
00:03:37,704 --> 00:03:39,188
Thanks for watching.

